    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Grammarly is a for-profit company founded in 2009 and headquartered in San Francisco, California. The company describes itself as providing AI writing assistance, offering personalized guidance, text generation, and tone suggestions across apps and websites. Its site states that it does not sell or monetize user content, does not use it for advertising, and does not permit third-party service providers to train models on user content.\n\nThe company's two tracked products are Grammarly, a general writing and editing tool that reads document text broadly, and Grammarly for Education, an institutional product covering student data, FERPA compliance, and generative AI features. The company's site also references a product called Superhuman Go, described as delivering writing support alongside productivity agents intended to reduce back-and-forth communication. The site claims that organizations deploying Grammarly save an average of $5,000 per employee per year.\n\nThe held facts note 175 instances of California law exposure associated with the company, which is consistent with its San Francisco headquarters. No litigation cases or MCP server registrations are recorded in the current data.",
